IGCSE Physics 0625 — Interactive Bilingual Course
=================================================

This project is non-commercial (school / public-benefit use).


Third-party code and design influences
--------------------------------------

No source code from the projects below has been copied into this repository. Where
an approach was adopted, it was reimplemented; the credits are recorded here because
the ideas materially shaped this design.

* ChemAIForge — https://github.com/zhangifonly/ChemAIForge — MIT License
  Influence: pure-function simulation kernel with a rule registry, and the practice of
  attaching data-driven test probes to a content catalogue so every item is verified
  to actually work.

* mathviz ("数学之美") — https://github.com/zhangifonly/mathviz
  PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 — https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0
  Influence: the narration script data model (script → sections → lines, with lines
  able to drive the visualisation), and the pre-build content integrity check.

  NOTE: PolyForm Noncommercial permits non-commercial use only. This project is
  non-commercial, so the influence is compatible. Should this project ever become
  commercial, that status must be re-examined and, if any mathviz code is introduced,
  a commercial licence obtained from its authors. Any such code must be isolated
  under src/vendor/mathviz/ so it can be identified or removed cleanly. As of this
  writing, no mathviz code is present.

* edulab — https://github.com/wy51ai/edulab — Apache License 2.0
  Influence: the content-generation discipline of computing values exactly in a
  kernel and then self-checking that the kernel's answer equals the value displayed
  to the student.

* physics.whaty.org, bio.whaty.org, synthoming.whaty.org (closed-source websites)
  Influence: lesson page information architecture; and, from SynthoMing, the
  progressive content-depth switcher and the layered audio fallback chain
  (pre-generated file → generic file → browser speech synthesis).

* LearningCell — https://github.com/GordenSun/LearningCell
  No licence is declared, so all rights are reserved by its authors. No code or
  asset from this project may be used here. Referenced for inspiration only.

* "物理学与现代生活" — https://github.com/CrazyRock114/physics
  A republication of the assets of physics-app-*.tcloudbaseapp.com. Its own README
  states that copyright in the data and implementation remains with the original
  author and that the repository exists for study and local demonstration only.
  No licence is declared, so all rights are reserved. No code or data from it is used
  here.
  Influence: its per-simulation data contract independently validated the
  content-as-data approach used in src/content/. Two ideas were adopted and
  reimplemented from scratch: one-click scenario presets (`SimSpec.presets`) and a
  short on-canvas instruction telling the student what is draggable (`SimSpec.hint`).

* "Science_Math" — https://github.com/CrazyRock114/Science_Math
  Self-contained per-topic HTML lessons for primary and middle school. No licence is
  declared, so all rights are reserved. No code from it is used here.
  Influence: its lever demonstration suggested the live equation that states its own
  outcome — rendering "3.92 = 3.92 N m ⇒ balanced" or "8.82 > 2.94 N m ⇒ left sinks"
  rather than a bare pair of readouts. Implemented here through the optional
  `EquationBlock.substitute` hook.


